9/", "id": 476032579, "docket": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/dockets/73670930/", "recap_documents": [{"resource_uri": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/recap-documents/491582619/", "id": 491582619, "tags": [], "absolute_url": "", "date_created": "2026-08-27T10:35:32.857168-07:00", "date_modified": "2026-08-27T10:35:32.857189-07:00", "sha1": "", "page_count": null, "file_size": null, "filepath_local": null, "filepath_ia": "", "ia_upload_failure_count": null, "thumbnail": null, "thumbnail_status": 0, "plain_text": "", "ocr_status": null, "date_upload": null, "document_number": "", "attachment_number": null, "pacer_doc_id": "", "is_available": false, "is_free_on_pacer": null, "is_sealed": null, "document_type": 1, "description": "Set Deadlines/Hearings", "acms_document_guid": ""}], "date_created": "2026-08-27T10:35:32.843105-07:00", "date_modified": "2026-08-27T10:35:32.843131-07:00", "date_filed": "2026-08-27", "time_filed": "10:27:22", "entry_number": null, "recap_sequence_number": "2026-08-27.001", "pacer_sequence_number": null, "description": "", "tags": []}, {"resource_uri": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/docket-entries/475877112/", "id": 475877112, "docket": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/dockets/73670930/", "recap_documents": [{"resource_uri": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/recap-documents/491423510/", "id": 491423510, "tags": [], "absolute_url": "/docket/73670930/25/in-re-claude-service-degradation-litigation/", "date_created": "2026-08-26T11:34:16.495456-07:00", "date_modified": "2026-08-26T22:43:59.236343-07:00", "sha1": "783fe2dfd479886363c35b38d4a31d25c2be9631", "page_count": 3, "file_size": 175598, "filepath_local": "recap/gov.uscourts.cand.474951/gov.uscourts.cand.474951.25.0.pdf", "filepath_ia": "", "ia_upload_failure_count": null, "thumbnail": null, "thumbnail_status": 0, "plain_text": "       Case 3:26-cv-07699-RFL             Document 25          Filed 08/26/26   Page 1 of 3\n\n\n\n\n                                  UNITED STATES DISTRICT COURT\n\n                                 NORTHERN DISTRICT OF CALIFORNIA\n\n\n                                                         ORDER GRANTING PLAINTIFFS\u2019\n  ISABELO PASCUAL,                                       UNOPPOSED MOTION TO\n                    Plaintiff,                           CONSOLIDATE; DENYING\n                                                         WITHOUT PREJUDICE THE\n            v.                                           MOTION TO APPOINT INTERIM\n                                                         COUNSEL\n  ANTHROPIC, PBC,\n                    Defendant.                           Case No. 26-cv-07699-RFL\n                                                         Re: Dkt. No. 24\n\n  MONEAL PATEL et al.,\n                    Plaintiffs,                           Case No. 26-cv-07837-RFL\n                                                          Re: Dkt. No. 25\n            v.\n\n  ANTHROPIC, PBC,\n                    Defendant.\n\n\n\n\n       For good cause shown, Plaintiffs Isabelo Pascual, Moneal Patel, and Laurel Morgan\n\n(collectively, \u201cPlaintiffs\u201d) Unopposed Motion to Consolidate Related Actions is GRANTED.\n\nAccordingly, the Court ORDERS as follows:\n\n       1.        Pascual v. Anthropic, PBC, No. 4:26-cv-07699-RFL and Patel v. Anthropic, PBC,\n\n                 No. 3:26-cv-07837-RFL, shall be consolidated under the Pascual case, pursuant to\n\n                 Federal Rule of Civil Procedure 42(a) (the \u201cConsolidated Action\u201d);\n\n       2.        All papers in the Consolidated Action shall be filed under Case No. 26-cv-07699,\n                 and shall bear the following caption:\n\n\n\n                                                   1\n\fCase 3:26-cv-07699-RFL               Document 25      Filed 08/26/26          Page 2 of 3\n\n\n\n\n     IN RE CLAUDE SERVICE\n                                                        Master File No. 26-cv-07699-RFL\n     DEGRADATION LITIGATION\n\n     This Document Relates To:\n\n3.       The case file for the Consolidated Action will be maintained under Master File\n\n         No. 4:26-cv-07699. When a pleading is intended to apply to all actions to which\n\n         this Order applies, the words \u201cAll Actions\u201d shall appear immediately after the\n\n         words \u201cThis Document Relates To:\u201d in the caption described above. When a\n\n         pleading is not intended to apply to all actions, the docket number for each\n\n         individual action to which the paper is intended to apply and the last name of the\n\n         first-named plaintiff in said action shall appear immediately after the words, \u201cThis\n\n         Document Relates To:\u201d in the caption identified above, e.g., \u201c4:26-cv-07699\n\n         (Pascual).\u201d\n\n4.       Any other action arising out of the same or similar operative facts and seeking\n\n         relief on class or representative basis now pending or hereafter filed in, removed\n\n         to, or transferred to this District, and which the Court finds related to the\n\n         Consolidated Action, shall be consolidated for pre-trial purposes pursuant to Rule\n\n         42(a). The parties shall file a Notice of Related Action whenever a case that they\n\n         believe should be consolidated into this action is filed in, transferred to, or\n\n         removed to this District.\n\n5.       If the Court determines that the case is related, the clerk shall:\n\n            a. Place a copy of this Order in the separate file for such action;\n\n            b. Serve on Plaintiffs\u2019 counsel in the new case a copy of this Order;\n\n            c. Direct that this Order be served upon Defendant(s) in the new case; and\n\n            d. Make appropriate entry in the Master Docket.\n6.       This Order shall apply to the above-captioned matters and any subsequently\n\n\n\n\n                                            2\n\f        Case 3:26-cv-07699-RFL           Document 25          Filed 08/26/26    Page 3 of 3\n\n\n\n\n               consolidated actions.\n\n       Plaintiffs shall file a Consolidated Amended Complaint by September 12, 2026.\n\n       The Motion to Appoint Interim Counsel is DENIED without prejudice as premature. If a\n\nsignificant number of additional cases are added to the Consolidated Action, Plaintiffs may\n\nrenew their request for appointment of interim class counsel. Otherwise, appointment of class\n\ncounsel will be addressed at the class certification stage.\n\n\n\n       IT IS SO ORDERED.\n\nDated: August 26, 2026\n\n\n\n\n                                                                RITA F. LIN\n                                                                United States District Judge\n\n\n\n\n                                                  3\n\f", "ocr_status": 2, "date_upload": "2026-08-26T22:43:59.209742-07:00", "document_number": "25", "attachment_number": null, "pacer_doc_id": "035027559605", "is_available": true, "is_free_on_pacer": null, "is_sealed": null, "document_type": 1, "description": "Order on Motion to Consolidate Cases AND Order on Motion to Consolidate Cases", "acms_document_guid": ""}], "date_created": "2026-08-26T11:34:16.432345-07:00", "date_modified": "2026-08-26T11:34:16.443242-07:00", "date_filed": "2026-08-26", "time_filed": "11:29:52", "entry_number": 25, "recap_sequence_number": "2026-08-26.001", "pacer_sequence_number": 74, "description": "", "tags": []}, {"resource_uri": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/docket-entries/475251650/", "id": 475251650, "docket": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/dockets/73670930/", "recap_documents": [{"resource_uri": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/recap-documents/490777911/", "id": 490777911, "tags": [], "absolute_url": "/docket/73670930/24/in-re-claude-service-degradation-litigation/", "date_created": "2026-08-20T14:02:59.486453-07:00", "date_modified